<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Chalcidian League</h1><p class="st-meta">432 BCE – 348 BCE · capital Olynthus</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Federation of the Greek towns of Chalcidice centred on Olynthus, the strongest power of the northern Aegean until Philip II of Macedon destroyed it.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 432 BCE the Chalcidian towns, persuaded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perdiccas-ii-of-macedon">Perdiccas II of Macedon</a>, revolted from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/delian-league">Delian League</a>, and many of their people moved into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/olynthus">Olynthus</a>. From this union grew a federal state calling itself 'the Chalcidians'. With help from the Spartan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brasidas">Brasidas</a> in 424 BCE it secured its independence from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/athens">Athens</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Member towns shared citizenship, laws on marriage and property and a common <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> coinage showing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> and his lyre, among the finest of the age. In the early 4th century BCE the league grew aggressively, absorbing <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/potidaea">Potidaea</a> and even occupying <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pella">Pella</a>, the Macedonian capital, during the troubles of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amyntas-iii-of-macedon">Amyntas III</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Appeals from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acanthus-greece">Acanthus</a> and Apollonia brought a Spartan war (382-379 BCE) that forced the league to dissolve. It revived, allied first with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II</a> and then with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/athens">Athens</a>, but Philip besieged <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/olynthus">Olynthus</a> and destroyed it in 348 BCE, ending the league and annexing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalcidice">Chalcidice</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/chalcidian-league.jpg" alt="Chalcidian League" width="320" height="163"><figcaption>Image: cgb · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:T%C3%A9tradrachme_de_la_ligue_chalcidique_%C3%A0_l%27effigie_d%27Apollon_et_de_sa_lyre.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>432 BCE – 348 BCE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Olynthus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ancient Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Chalcidian Confederacy, Chalkidians of Thrace</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-390&amp;focus=chalcidian-league" aria-label="Chalcidian League on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5254 737 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Chalcidian League lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5574 993L5574 993M5574 993L5562 1098M5574 993L5548 987"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5574 993h0M5562 1098h0M5548 987h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5574 993h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5574 993h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Olynthus. <a href="/atlas?year=-390&amp;focus=chalcidian-league">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

